{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.GramQuotientDetD","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramQuotientDetD","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Symmetric","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Shared.DetFin","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L193-L200","doc":"**THEOREM.** The leading 5×5 minor of the canonical Gram is nonzero for\n**every real `q`** — so `gramMatrixD q` has rank exactly 5 and its radical\nis exactly the antisymmetriser direction, at every real `q`. This is the\nstatement that replaces `gramMatrix_det_ne_zero` in the canonical frame;\nits nonvanishing is basis-independent, unlike the value it is derived\nfrom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det_neg","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L172-L191","doc":"**THEOREM.** The quotient determinant is strictly negative for **every**\nreal `q` — no `q > 0`, no `q > 1`, no substrate hypothesis. Each factor of\nthe closed form is real-rootless: `q⁴+1 > 0`, `q²−q+1 = (q−½)²+¾ > 0`,\n`q²+q+1 = (q+½)²+¾ > 0`, `(q²+1)¹⁰ > 0`. So the nondegenerate quotient\nform is **indefinite**: any D-frame successor to the C-frame\npositive-definiteness reading must say \"nondegenerate\", never \"positive\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L159-L170","doc":"**MAIN THEOREM.** The determinant of the form induced on `H_3(q)/rad` by\nthe canonical Gram, in the complement basis `e_0, …, e_4`:\n\n  det( G_D | H_3/rad ) = −(q⁴+1)(q²−q+1)⁴(q²+q+1)⁴ / (q²+1)¹⁰ .\n\nThis is the convention-D replacement for the C-only\n`gramMatrix_det_ne_zero`. The value is basis-dependent (it moves by the\nsquare of a change-of-basis determinant); its nonvanishing is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det_mul_denom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_det_mul_denom","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L142-L157","doc":"**THEOREM (cleared form).** `(q²+1)¹⁰ · det(G_D | H_3/rad)` is the\ndegree-20 polynomial `−(q⁴+1)(q²−q+1)⁴(q²+q+1)⁴`.\n\nThe workhorse: `Matrix.det_fin_five` expands the determinant into its 120\nLeibniz terms, the entries are unfolded from `gramEntryD`, `field_simp`\nclears the `(q²+1)`-power denominators and `ring` closes the polynomial\nidentity. No hypothesis on `q`; default heartbeat budget suffices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_top_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_top_left","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L139-L140","doc":"**THEOREM.** `G[0,0] = tr_M(1) = 1` survives on the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_isSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_isSymm","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L133-L137","doc":"**THEOREM.** The quotient form is symmetric — inherited from\n`gramMatrixD_isSymm`, since a principal submatrix of a symmetric matrix is\nsymmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD_apply","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L129-L131","doc":"`gramQuotientD` is the leading block of `gramMatrixD`, entrywise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramQuotientD","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L121-L127","doc":"The form induced by the canonical (convention-D) Gram on `H_3(q)/rad`, in\nthe complement basis `e_0, …, e_4`: the leading `5×5` principal minor of\n`gramMatrixD q`, obtained as a `submatrix` along `Fin.castSucc`. The\nentries are **not** re-typed — everything below is derived from the\n36-entry table `gramEntryD`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramRadicalD_last","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramRadicalD_last","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/GramQuotientDetD.lean#L112-L119","doc":"**THEOREM.** The last coordinate of the radical direction is `1`.\n\nThis is what makes `e_0, …, e_4` a complement of the radical for every\n`q` (including `q = 0`), so that the quotient form may be read off the\nleading 5×5 principal minor. `gramRadicalD_ne_zero` used the same\ncoordinate; this states it as the equality the complement argument\nactually needs. ","signatureChunk":0}]}